[E0436] Error: `views` is used after `owned`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/197_built_list_borrows/main.wip:13:17 ]
    │
 11 │     val views: own<[str]> = own [owned.toStr(), if true { yield "x" }]
    │         ──┬──  
    │           ╰──── `views` borrows `owned`
 12 │     owned.clear()
    │     ──┬──  
    │       ╰──── `owned` passed as `&var` here
 13 │     io::println(views[0])
    │                 ──┬──  
    │                   ╰──── used here
    │ 
    │ Help: use `views` before `owned` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │ 
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
